commit 2c986930b352f2f2b66f12768f6c428818ad9ac1

C03: symbolic public names get their canonical destination; confirmed replies compose against the request (WEB1259 repair)

WEB1257 measured two causes: «andá a youtube», «llevame a github» and
«Ve a ChatGPT» planned a single browser.navigate (the Start catalog knows
those names, so no search) but the argument builder abstained before the
symbolic destination and the App asked for a URL; and a reply published
after the closed word «confirmar» composed against it («Sí, confirmo que
se navegó…»). The builder now accepts the closed public list the reader
already relies on, and the view model composes such replies against the
last user message that is not a confirmation reply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


